Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:55:56 +0800
Subject: media: histb-vpss: rotate through a two-image chain


Rotation is the last capability with a block path behind it, and one
job carrying the port's crop, letterbox, scaler and timeout delivers
only the first strip.

The rotate shape that does work writes one image per plane --
IMG_PRO_MODE 1 for luma and 2 for chroma, ROTATE_EN with the angle
bit selecting the direction, the whole frame in and the swapped frame
out -- and chains the two by PNEXT with START on both.

Write the chain that way and refuse the combinations it cannot model
(crop, sharpening, flips, chroma-order swap, a 4:2:2 quarter turn),
accept back the compose rectangle G_SELECTION reports because nothing
smaller is deliverable, let a requested flip cancel the matching half
of a turn instead of being overwritten, and fix the reset path so it
reports failure, the driver refuses jobs once a reset faulted or while
it is removing, and a pitch wider than the block can address is
rejected.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 2 files changed, 419 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)


